1 NOTE FULL NAME "LOUISE MAXIMILIENNE CAROLINE EMANUELE"; "OF STOLBERG"; COUNTESS OF
2 CONT ALBANY
1 NOTE Albany, Louisa, countess of, 1752-1824, wife of Charles Edward Stuart (the Young Pretender), self-styled count of Albany; daughter of a German noble, the prince of Stolberg-Gedern. Married in 1772, she was made unhappy by her diss
2 CONC olute husband, left him after eight years, and became the mistress of the poet Vittorio Alfieri until his death in 1803. After that she was thte mistress of a French artist, François Fabre. Secret marriages with both men were rumo
2 CONC red, but not well attested. See biography by Margaret Mitchiner (1937). [The Illustrated Columbia Encyclopedia, 1969]
