2 CONT BIOGRAPHY The Almanach de Gotha (1873 edition, page 198) refers to Friedrich V as Prince (Fürst de Salm-Kyrbourg, prince d'Ahaus et Bocholt, wildgrave et rhingrave, comte de Rennenbourg, grand d'Espagne de 1ère classe, and son of 
2 CONC Prince Friedrich V and Princesse Cécile Rosalie, baronne de Borderaux. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As both Friedrich V and his son Friedrich VI were Fürst zu Salm-Kyrburg, obviously Europaische Stammtafeln is in error in declaring the 1815 marriage as morganatic. It appears that in 1815 the marriage of Friedrich IV and Cécile P
2 CONC révôt was declared to be an equal marriage.
