2 DATE 16 FEB 1898
1 OCCU French Jesuit and literato
1 TITL rev.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Father Alexandre de Cadoine de Gabriac, born in Rio de Janeiro on September 6, 1827, and died on February 16, 1898, was a French Jesuit and litterateur.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Ernest de Cadoine de Gabriac, an ambassador of Charles-Philippe of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Choosing the ecclesiastical state, he was ordained priest in 1852 and taught humanities.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rector of the College of Le Mans from 1871 to 1874, of the College of Saint-Ignace in Paris from 1874 to 1882 and from 1886 to 1889, of the College Saint-François-de-Sales in Evreux from 1882 to 1886, Spiritual Father at the resid
2 CONC ence of Saint-Germain in Paris from 1889 to 1890, Superior of Rouen from 1890 to 1896.
2 CONT
2 CONT Works:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Need for written disclosure
2 CONT * The Death of the Just, or the Vengeance of a Woman, tragedy in 5 acts and in verse (1848)
2 CONT * The Reverend Father A. de Ponlevoy of the Society of Jesus: his life; with a choice of pamphlets and letters. Ascetic pamphlets (1877)
2 CONT * Saint-François-de-Sales Institution (1883)
2 CONT * François de Guise, drama in 3 acts and in verse (1890)
2 CONT * Prince Bismarck and Alsace-Lorraine
2 CONT * Notes and references 
2 CONT * "National dictionary of contemporaries: containing notices from members of the Institut de France, the French government and parliament, the Academy of Medicine... Volume 3, edited by C.-E. Curinier (p. 65)", General publishing 
2 CONC office. bookstore and printing. (Paris) - 1899-1919.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Serafim Leite, "História Da Companhia de Jesus No Brasil, Volume 6", 2006
2 CONT * Marie de Flavigny , "General correspondence, Volume 1; Volumes 1821 to 1936", 2003
2 CONT * "Revista do Instituto Histórico e Geográfico Brasileiro", 1978
2 CONT * “Verbum, Volumes 1 to 2”, Universidade Católica do Rio de Janeiro, 1944
2 CONT * László Polgár , "Bibliography on the history of the Society of Jesus", 1990
2 CONT * Jaime del Burgo, "Bibliografía del siglo XIX: guerras carlistas, luchas políticas", 1978
2 CONT * “Library of Writers of the Society of Jesus or Bibliographic Notices”
2 CONT * "The House of Polignac: study of a social evolution of the nobility", 1975
2 CONT * "The Catholic University...", 1913
