1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Robert Maule Ramsay
2 CONT
2 CONT Naval Attaché to Paris between 1919 and 1922. Commander of the H.M.S. Dunedin in 1922. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Commodore of the Royal Naval Barracks, Portsmouth between 1929 and 1931.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Naval Aide-de-Camp to HM King George V in 1931.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rear-Admiral of the aircraft carriers between 1933 and 1936.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vice-Admiral in 1936.
2 CONT
2 CONT Commander-in-Chief of the East Indies between 1936 and 1938.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight Commander, Order of the Bath (K.C.B.) in 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight Grand Cross, Royal Victorian Order (G.C.V.O.) in 1938.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Admiral in 1938.3 He held the office of Fifth Sea Lord between 1938 and 1939.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fought in the First World War, where he was mentioned in despatches, decorated with the award of Companion, Distinguished Service Order (D.S.O.) in 1916.and the award of Legion of Honour
