1 NAME Charles Antoine Marie Louis Eugène Lamoral /de Ligne de La Trémoïlle/ prince de Ligne
2 GIVN Charles Antoine Marie Louis Eugène Lamoral
2 NSFX prince de Ligne
2 _MARNM de Ligne de La Trémoïlle
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 SEP 1946
2 ADDR
3 CITY Boulogne-Billancourt
3 STAE Île-de-France
3 CTRY France
1 OCCU Prince of Ligne-La Trémoille, Full Name: "Charles-Antoine Marie Louis Eugène Lamoral"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * See [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_Charles-Antoine_Lamoral_of_Ligne-La_Tr%C3%A9mo%C3%AFlle '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Prince Charles-Antoine Marie Louis Eugène Lamoral of Ligne-La Trémoïlle (born 30 September 1946) co-founded a company, Larex, Inc., that promoted development along the riverfront of the Los Angeles River corridor, including a poss
2 CONC ible high-speed train from San Francisco to San Diego.
2 CONT
2 CONT Background:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles-Antoine was born in Boulogne-sur-Mer, France, in 1946. He studied law at the Institut Catholique de Paris and hotel administration and management at Cornell University. He is the son of the late Prince Jean Charles of Lign
2 CONC e-La Trémoïlle and Maria del Rosario de Lambertye-Gerbeviller. He is third cousin once removed of Michel, head of the House of Ligne through their shared descent from Eugène, 8th Prince of Ligne. Like all members of the Ligne fami
2 CONC ly, he holds the title of prince in the Belgian nobility and the style of Altesse.
2 CONT
2 CONT His branch of the Ligne family are heirs in the female line of the House of La Trémoïlle, which held the rare rank of prince étranger during France's ancien régime, as pretenders to the crown of Naples. He is also a potential clai
2 CONC mant to the Kingdom of Jerusalem, together with Juan Carlos I, Louis Alphonse, Duke of Anjou, Victor Emmanuel, Prince of Naples, Otto von Habsburg, Infante Carlos, Duke of Calabria, Prince Carlo, Duke of Castro and Patrick Guinnes
2 CONC s. He is also a potential claimant to the Kingdom of Cyprus and the Armenian Kingdom of Cilicia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children:
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Lady Moira Beatrice Forbes, daughter of Arthur Forbes, 9th Earl of Granard and Marie Madeleine de Faucigny-Lucinge (descendant through an illegitimate branch of Charles X of France), on 7 October 1971 and were
2 CONC  divorced in 1975. He married, secondly, Princess Alyette Isabelle Odile Marie of Croÿ, daughter of Prince Rodolphe of Croÿ, and Odile de Bailleul, on 23 January 1976. they had two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * HH Prince Edouard Lamoral Rodolphe of Ligne (b. Paris, 27 September 1976) who married civilly on September 2, 2009 and religiously on September 5 2009, Italian actress Isabella Orsini.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * HH Prince Charles Lamoral Joseph Malcolm of Ligne (b. Paris, 25 February 1980)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles-Antoine_Lamoral,_prince_de_Ligne_de_La_Tr%C3%A9mo%C3%AFlle
2 CONT
