2 CONT http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Historia_%C5%81a%C5%84cuta
2 CONT
2 CONT The Potocki family was not persecuted by the Germans during World War II , and Łańcut castle housed the Wehrmacht headquarters . Before the entry of the Red Army on August 1, 1944, Alfred Potocki managed to escape to the West and,
2 CONC  with the Germans' permission, took away many of the castle's properties. Łańcut castle was not damaged during the hostilities of World War II.
