2 TITL Alfred Antoni Potocki, 4th ordinary of Łańcut, during his trip to north Africa at the end of the 1920s.
2 NOTE Alfred Antoni Potocki, 1920s. Photograph depicting Alfred Antoni Potocki, 4th ordinary of Łańcut, during his trip to north Africa at the end of the 1920s. Alfred Potocki is standing, wearing a grey suit, tie, and a shirt, and a ha
3 CONC t, on a large coconut door mat, leaning on a cane at the entrance to a hotel (?). Beside him, there is a young woman, wearing glasses, a dark hat with a large brim, and white attire, with a coat on her right arm; her right hand ho
3 CONC lds two brushes. On the right side of the ordinary, in the background, a step higher, stands a young, smiling man from the hotel personnel (?). In the background, a large door opening with a large grated overdoor window. Aldona Ch
3 CONC olewianka-Kruszyńska
