1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://peeragenews.blogspot.com/2014/07/mary-duchess-of-roxburghe-1915-2014.html
2 CONT
2 CONT "I was born in the United Kingdom and lived most of my life in Southern Africa. I was educated at Eton and studied at Christ Church, Oxford. I was first married to Isobel and married secondly Susan Mary Joclyn Semple of Kenya 
2 CONT
2 CONT I took an active interest in politics. In the 1930s I attended a Nuremberg Rally. I was a Member of Parliament at the break up of the Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland. I am one of the signatories of the Rhodesian Declaration o
2 CONC f Independence, signed in Salisbury, on November 11, 1965. I signed it 'Montrose'. I had cabinet portfolios as Minister of Agriculture and latterly Minister of Defence in Ian Smith's Rhodesian Front government.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several years later, in a dispute with Smith over the negotiations between the South African Government and Rhodesia regarding Black Majority Rule for Rhodesia, I resigned from the cabinet, and from government. My family and I mov
2 CONC ed to South Africa in 1979 and then to Scotland where I spent his final days. Always a keen Gaelic speaker with a great fondness for the Highlands and islands of Scotland, I lye buried in the family cemetery near Loch Lomond."
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Graham,_7th_Duke_of_Montrose
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p8091.htm
