1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacobo_Fitz-James_Stuart,_17th_Duke_of_Alba
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacobo_Fitz-James_Stuart,_17th_Duke_of_Alba
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Jacobo Fitz-James Stuart y Falcó, 17th Duke of Alba de Tormes, Grandee of Spain (17 October 1878 – 24 September 1953) was a Spanish noble, diplomat, politician and art collector. He was one of the most important aristocrats of
2 CONC  his time, and held, among other titles, the Dukedoms of Alba de Tormes and Berwick, the Countship of Lemos, Lerín and Montijo and the Marquessate of Carpio. He was also a Knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece of Spain in 1926.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early years
2 CONT
2 CONT He carried out his first studies under private tutors, but was later sent to England to study at Beaumont College, followed by Eton. After returning to Spain and concluding his school days at San Isidro, he continued with his high
2 CONC er education enrolling in the Universidad Central de Madrid, were he obtained his bachelor's degree in Law. Diplomatic career
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as Lord of the Bedchamber to the young King Alfonso XIII, who had acceded on his birth. In May 1902 royal visitors came to Madrid for the festivities to mark the King´s birthday and enthronement. The duke received the Kn
2 CONC ight Grand Cross of the Royal Victorian Order (GCVO) from the Duke of Connaught who was present for the festivities.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 2 February 1930 and 18 February 1931 Alba was Foreign Minister in Spain. During the Spanish Civil War, the Communists occupied his residence, the Palace of Liria (which his daughter later restored), and murdered his younge
2 CONC r brother Hernando Carlos Maria Theresa FitzJames Stuart y Falco (1882-1936). Alba became General Franco's official representative in London. He was still the Ambassador there in 1939, when Neville Chamberlain's cabinet formally g
2 CONC ave Franco's Nationalists diplomatic recognition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following World War II, Alba's relations with Franco markedly cooled, the result of Alba supporting a prompt monarchist restoration much more than Franco did. He was a leading guest at the 1947 wedding of Princess Elizabeth and Ph
2 CONC ilip, Duke of Edinburgh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olympic career
2 CONT
2 CONT He won a silver medal in the 1920 Olympic Games polo event.
