2 CONT Personal details
2 CONT Born	James Hubert Ramsay
2 CONT 17 January 1948 (age 76)
2 CONT Political party	Conservative
2 CONT Spouse	Marilyn Butter ​(m. 1973)​
2 CONT Children	3
2 CONT Parent(s)	Simon Ramsay, 16th Earl of Dalhousie
2 CONT Margaret Stirling
2 CONT Education	Ampleforth College
2 CONT James Hubert Ramsay, 17th Earl of Dalhousie, GCVO, DL (born 17 January 1948), styled Lord Ramsay between 1950 and 1999, is a Scottish peer, courtier and landowner. He is chief of Clan Ramsay and Deputy Captain General of the King'
2 CONC s Body Guard for Scotland. In that role, he took part in the Royal Procession at the Coronation of Charles III and Camilla.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Early life and education
2 CONT Dalhousie was born on 17 January 1948, the son of Simon Ramsay, later 16th Earl of Dalhousie, and his wife Margaret Elizabeth Mary Stirling (1914–1997). His mother was a sister of Sir David Stirling, founder of the Special Air Ser
2 CONC vice, and therefore (a descendant of Charles II). He was educated at Ampleforth College.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1968, Dalhousie, then styled Lord Ramsay, trained at the Mons Officer Cadet School and was commissioned as a second lieutenant into the Coldstream Guards.[2] In 1971 he transferred from the active list to the Regular Army Reser
2 CONC ve of Officers.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT Dalhousie had a career in investment banking.[4] On 15 July 1999, his father died and he succeeded to the earldom of Dalhousie as the 17th Earl. He briefly sat in the House of Lords as a Conservative, he lost his seat four months 
2 CONC later with the passing of the House of Lords Act 1999.[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dalhousie was appointed Lord Steward of Household on 22 July 2009 on the retirement of the 5th Duke of Abercorn.[7] He relinquished his appointment on 22 February 2023 and was succeeded by the 7th Earl of Rosslyn.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT He has been Vice Lord-Lieutenant of Angus since 10 December 2002.[9][10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT On 3 October 1973, the then Lord Ramsay married Marilyn Davina Butter (born 22 March 1950), second daughter of Sir David and Lady Butter, at the Guards' Chapel, Wellington Barracks.[11] They have three children:[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Lorna Theresa Ramsay (born 6 February 1975), married Fergus Lefebvre in 2005, has issue
2 CONT Lady Alice Magdalene Ramsay (born 10 August 1977), married Michael Dickinson, has issue
2 CONT Simon David Ramsay, Lord Ramsay (born 18 April 1981), married Kaitlin Kubinsky in 2016, has issue
2 CONT In 2019, he listed Brechin Castle, the family seat in Angus, for sale through Savills.[12][13][14][15] Lord and Lady Dalhousie moved to a small house of the estate, which they retained most of.[16] Much of the family's immovable p
2 CONC roperties have been vested into Dalhousie Estates, a family-run business engaged in farming, property letting and forestry, including shooting, fishing and deer stalking. The business venture provides employment for over 90 people
2 CONC .[17]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Dalhousie is a patroness of the Royal Caledonian Ball.[18]
2 CONT
2 CONT Honours
2 CONT  17 January 2012: Commander (Brother) of the Most Venerable Order of the Hospital of Saint John of Jerusalem (CStJ)[19]
2 CONT  25 March 2023: Knight Grand Cross of the Royal Victorian Order (GCVO)[20]
2 CONT Honorary military appointments
2 CONT United Kingdom 1 June 2008: Honorary Captain, His Majesty's Royal Naval Reserve[21]
2 CONT Arms
2 CONT Coat of arms of James Ramsay, 17th Earl of Dalhousie 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Coronet
2 CONT A Coronet of an Earl
2 CONT Crest
2 CONT An Unicorn's Head couped at the neck armed maned and tufted Or
2 CONT Escutcheon
2 CONT Argent an Eagle displayed Sable beaked and membered Gules
2 CONT Supporters
2 CONT On the dexter side a Griffin Argent, and on the sinister side a Greyhound Argent gorged with a Collar Gules charged with three Escallops of the first
2 CONT Motto
2 CONT Ora Et Labora (Pray and work!)
2 CONT
