1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_of_Alba
2 CONT
2 CONT '''María del Rosario Cayetana Paloma Alfonsa Victoria Eugenia Fernanda Teresa Francisca de Paula Lourdes Antonia Josefa Fausta Rita Castor Dorotea Santa Esperanza Fitz-James Stuart y de Silva Falcó y Gurtubay, 18th Duchess of Alba
2 CONC  de Tormes, Grandee of Spain''' (28 March 1926 – 20 November 2014) was the head of the House of Alba and the third woman to carry the title in her own right.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born at Liria Palace on 28 March 1926, as the only child of the 17th Duke of Alba (a prominent politician and diplomat during the 1930s and 1940s), and his wife, María del Rosario de Silva y Gurtubay, 9th Marchioness of Sa
2 CONC n Vicente del Barco. Her godmother was the Queen Consort of Spain, Victoria Eugenie of Battenberg, King of Spain Alfonso XIII de Borbón’s wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT The matriarch’s senior title was Duchess of Alba, but she had more than 40 others. According to Guinness World Records, she had more titles recognized by an existing government than any other noble in the world.
2 CONT
2 CONT As the male-preference primogeniture from James FitzJames, she also claimed the title of Duchess of Berwick. She was a direct descendant of the King James II of Great Britain, through his illegitimate son James FitzJames, 1st Duke
2 CONC  of Berwick by his mistress Arabella Churchill.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-2045627/Duchess-Alba-marries-toyboy-Alfonso-Diez-lavish-wedding-ceremony.html  _20.11.2014_
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayetana_Fitz-James_Stuart,_18th_Duchess_of_Alba
2 CONT
2 CONT Doña María del Rosario Cayetana Fitz-James Stuart y de Silva, 18th Duchess of Alba de Tormes, Grandee of Spain (28 March 1926 – 20 November 2014), was head of the House of Alba and the third woman to hold the dukedom of Alba in he
2 CONC r own right.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Liria Palace on 28 March 1926, she was the only child of the 17th Duke of Alba (a prominent Spanish politician and diplomat during the 1930s and 1940s) by his wife, María del Rosario de Silva y Gurtubay, 9th Marchioness of
2 CONC  San Vicente del Barco. Her godmother was the Queen Victoria Eugenie, wife of King Alfonso XIII of Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT As head of the dynasty, she was styled by her most senior title of "Duchess of Alba", whilst holding over 40 other hereditary titles. According to Guinness World Records, she was the most titled aristocrat in the world.
2 CONT
2 CONT Via her descent from James FitzJames, she was King James II of England's senior illegitimate-line descendant. She was inducted into Vanity Fair's International Best Dressed List Hall of Fame in 2011.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life and family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayetana_Fitz-James_Stuart,_18th_Duchess_of_Alba#Life_and_family
